1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,400
Why Domain Matters, part 1: Retail and grocery. 5 kg atta sales fell 59% in a week; the shelf was empty for 39 open hours.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:10,300
Each post takes one failure, shows what the data made of it, and scores it against what really happened.

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:17,200
Monday’s review: sales down 59%. The AI assistant, given the warehouse schema, blames shoppers switching packs.

4
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:23,600
11 of 12 data tests pass. Four tests about how a store works all fail, on the same records.

5
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:30,500
What happened: the cases sat behind the rice for 39 open hours. The books never fell to the reorder point.

6
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,900
The demo: change what the data team does with June’s records, or rerun June with the store acting on what it finds.

7
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:44,300
The gap detector, hour by hour: blue hours are censored, yellow is the answer key’s empty shelf. It flags 5 kg atta at 19:00 on Wednesday.

8
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:51,200
At 1 in 100 it finds 7 of 10 gaps, but only 7 of 23 alerts are real. At 1 in 1,000: 6 gaps, 6 of 10. The threshold is a business decision.

9
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:58,600
Unconstrained, the forecast holds at 25.6 bags a day. Scored on recorded sales it looks worse: +22% against +13%.

10
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:06,000
With a domain layer the assistant answers 7 of 7, and finds the silence, the audit that saw the empty bay, and no delivery.

11
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,900
Rerun June with a check at every alert: the gap ends the same evening, and 35 bags are lost instead of 157.

12
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:19,300
One name, five numbers: availability of 97%, 75% or 79% from the records; 77% or 78% from the answer key.

13
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:25,200
Or capture the missing event: scan every case into a backroom bin, and 1 bag is lost instead of 157.

14
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:31,600
The technical companion: the tests in SQL, the detector and the forecast in Python, every query the assistant ran, and a notebook.

15
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:38,000
For data and AI leaders: five questions to ask your team.

16
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,500
Sales are not demand. And book stock is a belief, not the shelf.
